.TH VELOCITTY 1 "September 2026" "velocitty 0.2.0" "Velocitty Terminal Emulator"
.SH NAME
velocitty \- CPU-rendered terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B velocitty
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-e | \-\-
.IR command " [" arg "...]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B velocitty
is a CPU-rendered terminal emulator.
It is designed to keep up with high-volume output such as
.BR cat (1)
of large files: PTY input is truncated through a mirrored circular buffer,
split into lines and runs with SIMD, then fed to a minimal-state VT emulator
and drawn to a software framebuffer.
.PP
With no
.B \-e
command, the child is
.B $SHELL
(or
.B /bin/sh
if unset). The child environment sets
.BR TERM = xterm-256color
(SSH-safe terminfo),
.BR COLORTERM = truecolor ,
.BR TERM_PROGRAM = velocitty ,
and
.BR KITTY_WINDOW_ID
to the emulator PID.
.PP
Window class and title follow
.B \-\-class
/
.B \-\-title
and may be updated by OSC 176 and OSC 0/2. Geometry, font size, and inner
padding use CSS 96 DPI times a Hyprland /
.B GDK_SCALE
multiplier (not X11 millimetre DPI), reapplied on focus and resize only when
the scale or grid actually changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\- " " \fIcommand\fR " [" \fIarg\fR ...]
Execute
.I command
in the PTY instead of the shell. All following arguments are passed to
.IR command .
Must be last among options.
.TP
.BR \-\-class " " \fIname\fR
ICCCM / WM_CLASS instance name (also
.BR \-\-class= name ).
Default:
.BR velocitty .
.TP
.BR \-\-title " " \fItext\fR
Initial window title (also
.BR \-\-title= text ).
Default:
.BR Velocitty .
.TP
.BR \-\-working\-directory " " \fIdir\fR
Working directory of the child (also
.BR \-\-working\-directory= dir ).
Used by
.BR xdg-terminal-exec (1).
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the current selection to CLIPBOARD (UTF8_STRING).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V
Paste CLIPBOARD into the PTY (bracketed paste if DECSET 2004 is on).
.TP
.B Shift+Insert
Same as Ctrl+Shift+V.
.PP
Other keys are sent as VT sequences (including application-cursor keys when
the application has enabled them).
.SH MOUSE
Left-drag selects a cell stream. Double-click selects a word; triple-click
selects a line. Releasing the button copies the selection to PRIMARY.
.PP
When mouse reporting is enabled (DECSET 1000/1002/1003, SGR/urxvt/pixel
modes), Shift+drag still selects instead of reporting. Middle-click pastes
PRIMARY. Wheel events go to the application when reporting, otherwise scroll
the primary screen history or send arrow keys on the alternate screen.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Config is TOML, similar to Alacritty. Unknown keys are ignored.
.PP
Load order (later files overlay earlier; Omarchy theme colors win when
present):
.IP 1. 3
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/velocitty/config.toml
(default
.IR ~/.config/velocitty/config.toml )
.IP 2.
.I ./config.toml
in the current working directory
.IP 3.
Omarchy current theme
.I colors.toml
.IP 4.
Omarchy current theme
.I alacritty.toml
.PP
If
.B [font].size
is still unset, size is taken from
.IR ~/.config/alacritty/alacritty.toml ,
then 9 when an Omarchy theme is in use. Unset family is resolved with
fontconfig
.B monospace
.RB ( "omarchy font current" ).
.SS Colors
Root or
.B [colors]
/
.B [colors.primary]
keys:
.BR foreground " (" fg ),
.BR background " (" bg ),
.BR cursor .
.B [normal]
and
.B [bright]
(or
.BR [colors.normal] ,
.BR [colors.bright] )
set the 16 ANSI colors. Omarchy
.I colors.toml
keys such as
.BR muted ,
.BR bright_foreground ,
and root-level ANSI names are accepted.
.SS [general]
.TP
.BR refreshrate " / " hz
Target redraw rate in Hz when PTY reads return EAGAIN. Default: 30.
.TP
.B whitelist
If true, parse a whitelist of escape sequences during line split (payloads
may contain newline bytes). Default: false (split on newlines only).
.TP
.BR pad " / " padding
Inner window margin in CSS pixels, all sides. Default: 14. Scaled by the
output scale factor.
.SS [font]
.TP
.BR family " / " font " / " font_family
Fontconfig family name. Default: fontconfig
.BR monospace .
.TP
.BR size " / " font_size
Point size. Default: Alacritty config, else 9 under Omarchy, else the
built-in fallback fonts.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
.RS
foreground = "#ebdbb2"
background = "#282828"
cursor = "#ebdbb2"

[normal]
black = "#282828"
red = "#cc241d"
# ...

[bright]
black = "#928374"
# ...

[general]
refreshrate = 30
whitelist = false
pad = 14

[font]
family = "monospace"
size = 16
.RE
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate config, Omarchy state, and fontconfig.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides
.IR ~/.config
for user config and Alacritty overlay.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Overrides
.IR ~/.local/state
for Omarchy current theme paths.
.TP
.B SHELL
Child program when
.B \-e
is not given.
.TP
.B GDK_SCALE ", " QT_SCALE_FACTOR
UI scale fallback when Hyprland scale is unavailable.
.TP
.B TERM ", " COLORTERM ", " TERM_PROGRAM ", " KITTY_WINDOW_ID
Set in the child. Incoming
.B KITTY_LISTEN_ON
is cleared.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGUSR1 ", " SIGUSR2
Reload colors and font from config and the current Omarchy theme without
restarting. Theme/font file changes are also watched (throttled) and trigger
the same reload; CSI 2031 is sent when the palette changes.
.TP
.B SIGWINCH
Sent to the slave foreground process group after
.B TIOCSWINSZ
on resize.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/velocitty/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/omarchy/current/theme/colors.toml
.TQ
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/omarchy/current/theme/alacritty.toml
Omarchy live theme (overlaid on user config).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/alacritty/alacritty.toml
Font size fallback when unset.
.SH PROTOCOL
Implements a large subset of xterm / foot control sequences: C0/C1, ESC
charsets, CSI (SGR, CUP, DECSET/DECRQM, rectangular ops, kitty keyboard,
window ops, color stack, XTSMGRAPHICS), OSC (title, colors, OSC 8 hyperlinks,
cwd, notify, alpha, selection, cursor shape, OSC 52 clipboard, OSC 176
app-id), DCS (DECRQSS, iTerm sync, XTGETTCAP, sixel), and kitty graphics
(APC G, including
.B a=q
replies for icat).
.PP
DECSET 2026 and iTerm DCS
.B =1s
defer presenting frames until the synchronized update ends (1s timeout).
In-band resize (2048) flushes VT replies after a grid change.
.PP
In Debug builds only, OSC 556 and CSI
.B ? 556
toggle a visual overlay (grid, wrap, LCF, cursor, dirty, region, wide, HUD).
Ignored in Release.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xterm (1),
.BR foot (1),
.BR fc-match (1),
.BR xdg-terminal-exec (1)
.SH BUGS
macOS and Windows targets are not supported yet. There is no GPU renderer,
no multiplexer, and no kitty-style CTL.
